:answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69e8d5d4-178f-5213-b5c2-28dce17a3e6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234707} :answer-field/id #uuid "b43a43c9-923a-541f-b025-831b9fdeb66b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bd4e7b23-65ca-5e51-94d4-c72686633d86" :question/math-academy-id "q-168114" :question/problem "Find the partial derivatives of $\\text{div}\\,V$ at the point $(1,1).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n$\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\text{div}\\,V)\\,{|}_{(1,\\,1)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n$\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\text{div}\\,V)\\,{|}_{(1,\\,1)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\text{div}\\,V) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy+2x) \\\\  & =2y+2 \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\text{div}\\,V) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy+2x) \\\\  & =2x+0 \\\\  & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\text{div}\\,V)\\,{|}_{(1,\\,1)} & =2(1)+2 \\\\  & =4 \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\text{div}\\,V)\\,{|}_{(1,\\,1)} & =2(1) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235542 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bcf71f90-cbb8-5937-bf8c-aa426f84fa71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcf71f90-cbb8-5937-bf8c-aa426f84fa71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234835} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe580988-3de6-51d3-ad7e-b78106efb226" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0004c300-7b2f-5627-8c54-a9a44f3c9175" :question/math-academy-id "q-168862" :question/problem "$\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{y}^{4}-5{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+10{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}+2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{4})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(10{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{4})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(10{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the constant multiple rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{4})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(10{y}^{2}) & =-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{4})-5{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})+10\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-4{y}^{3}-5{x}^{2}\\cdot 2y+10\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25bb17e4-258b-51bf-91d3-7e60cc8a5b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266482} {:answer/id #uuid "3b886ea8-78ac-5785-a126-630c13002539" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266668} {:answer/id #uuid "90ef5240-d3e8-56bc-a359-94af08fe97cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267433} {:answer/id #uuid "d1666f3f-d78f-5b47-bf2e-cbd0ba0f6a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268015} {:answer/id #uuid "d92bf854-b63d-5ad5-821d-d64b45e82fe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90ef5240-d3e8-56bc-a359-94af08fe97cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267433} :answer-field/id #uuid "c37a1b95-6721-5ce6-92db-42984b088eeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1798a630-b3d2-5681-be69-eeaa1d664d97" :question/math-academy-id "q-132253" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(3,-1,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the constant multiple and chain rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2})}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}{({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2})}^{-1/2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}) & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4{z}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\cdot (2x+0) \\\\  & =\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4{z}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(3,-1,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(3,-1,-2)} & =\\frac{(3)(-1)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+4(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{9+16}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cbcfb89-b518-52f4-a378-bc4f54d231b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{2y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275879} {:answer/id #uuid "32c61380-4849-507d-b3b3-d576421fd9c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275927} {:answer/id #uuid "3e7cffcb-bc87-530f-a986-8f950f2b921b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276019} {:answer/id #uuid "8277d213-c7d3-506d-a625-8ce16ed02b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276653} {:answer/id #uuid "ca03764d-edf4-532a-81b1-cb8796cca4c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8277d213-c7d3-506d-a625-8ce16ed02b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276653} :answer-field/id #uuid "891d87b2-b404-5b6e-a0fe-b586955b1e92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "424001c9-342e-51ae-ba3f-40228db99e48" :question/math-academy-id "q-159656" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)={e}^{{x}^{2}y}-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}y}-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}y})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the chain and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}y})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot y\\cdot 2x-y\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =2xy{e}^{{x}^{2}y}-\\frac{y}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4008d421-bcc4-541e-b6d1-6f911e6c8d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2x\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276034} {:answer/id #uuid "430b88eb-d781-5955-bdd4-cba096425762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276071} {:answer/id #uuid "4fccdda9-5259-5b0d-9374-c4a4d5a9b18d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276193} {:answer/id #uuid "ba43033d-0504-5559-9fb4-0a81d932ee52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277130} {:answer/id #uuid "f142f4cb-083a-5c32-9524-ba93f1707e6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "430b88eb-d781-5955-bdd4-cba096425762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276071} :answer-field/id #uuid "05705cd0-c421-54fa-8117-fe18fa6f3bc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0833bc78-75ed-516b-b7f3-7df11e162117" :question/math-academy-id "q-159658" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{2xy-1}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the sum and the constant multiple rules for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy-1) & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}(2x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{2\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\cdot (2x\\cdot 1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2xy-1})}{\\sqrt{2xy-1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278245 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28d0f78d-518d-58c8-8c0b-81173c0184aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275847} {:answer/id #uuid "87e360c8-9939-5436-951b-6294befe5b85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276706} {:answer/id #uuid "b2eb3a7e-c309-596e-bc28-cb1b69bf6690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277079} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e642e7-633d-5cd9-a804-aa02d2102aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277097} {:answer/id #uuid "e08c2618-3181-5d40-a286-0a8436c4dcbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e08c2618-3181-5d40-a286-0a8436c4dcbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277439} :answer-field/id #uuid "dde4342f-9533-561d-aa12-ff6ee3bf5a50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2942efcf-e503-5d5c-b252-e682ffa52f18" :question/math-academy-id "q-159660" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),$ evaluate ${f}_{x}(\\frac{\\pi }{4},2).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the chain and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\cdot (2x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =2x{y}^{2}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(\\frac{\\pi }{4},2) & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot {2}^{2}+2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2\\pi +2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\  & =2\\pi +2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278246 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "124ba60a-ec47-5dd9-97fc-d33ccf7d0e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275645} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa03d48-f644-5066-b304-d3fc3f4f62eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276292} {:answer/id #uuid "5c6c70be-1878-50b5-989f-a8ed0e5f587f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276303} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b747a7-3b88-5c3b-b25b-53403f09d052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276925} {:answer/id #uuid "ec320ce3-f38d-5b16-8a80-a7b57185a46a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "124ba60a-ec47-5dd9-97fc-d33ccf7d0e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275645} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d4deb5e-7cf6-55ae-b93a-f09121cdee49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278004}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "95a36042-f58f-5fde-b6a7-7ca45f1d6809" :question/math-academy-id "q-159700" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x+y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{x+y}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}\\right) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)}{{sin}^{2}⁡y} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{sin}^{2}⁡y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{{sin}^{2}⁡y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(\\pi ,\\pi /2)} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-(\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)}{{sin}^{2}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-0}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8543754a-baf7-532f-9aaa-3f6e2f377989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276670} {:answer/id #uuid "872098d7-2da8-563d-9dbe-aa0ef1581439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276693} {:answer/id #uuid "9f76ba1c-fbca-5e67-ba0f-95af73b7592a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276912} {:answer/id #uuid "f00a4060-bf7f-5ccd-83cc-feaade45b7ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277585} {:answer/id #uuid "f0139e5c-4ac7-5bda-a049-12fd07049209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f00a4060-bf7f-5ccd-83cc-feaade45b7ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277585} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b4f281e-3538-5167-b8db-a9dda1fcb94e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8c6d2d99-f435-50ff-85c3-a966d3aa1af6" :question/math-academy-id "q-159709" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(0,2).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{x}{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\right) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\cdot (y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(0,2)} & =\\frac{2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-0\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{(2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+0}{(2+0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a420460-c7c1-505e-8ad4-c9bb108a6ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275860} {:answer/id #uuid "5f9d3b68-4176-5fa0-9407-0ed4c3eb41a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276332} {:answer/id #uuid "883a161b-2779-571d-bfa4-409b6a959feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276708} {:answer/id #uuid "b96f1c91-267d-539d-9fa8-52a5e328fc12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277120} {:answer/id #uuid "dfef293c-ea14-5c29-b5c4-17120a6c650d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b96f1c91-267d-539d-9fa8-52a5e328fc12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277120} :answer-field/id #uuid "af4b38e9-c4a5-5254-be14-837fef119079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c75dffc7-c60f-5338-92f4-7c0c6ff2bb72" :question/math-academy-id "q-159713" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{3x+y}{\\sqrt{x+y}}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{2(x+y)\\sqrt{x+y}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient and chain rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{3x+y}{\\sqrt{x+y}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3x+y)\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{x+y})}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+y))}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\cdot \\sqrt{x+y}-(3x+y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\cdot 1)}{{(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{6(x+y)-(3x+y)}{2\\sqrt{x+y}}\\right)}{x+y} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x+5y}{2(x+y)\\sqrt{x+y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=3x+5y.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278249 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1071740e-9558-5e73-b52c-d383864bf497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275622} {:answer/id #uuid "9e058e90-be98-5313-a164-e37b5eaec24f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-x{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276896} {:answer/id #uuid "b028380b-a597-535a-bd93-8b4c6734b700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277053} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6cb830-da03-564b-9a88-50ef70b7374f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+{x}^{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277142} {:answer/id #uuid "e1d0d589-d5cc-550b-974e-b4afdfaebb22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e058e90-be98-5313-a164-e37b5eaec24f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-x{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276896} :answer-field/id #uuid "75024153-b4e7-530d-be37-6a2d7adf8ab7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ad571fe8-149e-54b6-a89f-66ae79db7481" :question/math-academy-id "q-159714" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2x{y}^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}y}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{2h(x,y)}{{x}^{3}y}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{2x{y}^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}y}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot {x}^{2}y-(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)}{({x}^{2}y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}y-(2x{y}^{2}-1)\\cdot 2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}{y}^{3}-4{x}^{2}{y}^{3}+2xy}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy-2{x}^{2}{y}^{3}}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy(1-x{y}^{2})}{{x}^{4}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-x{y}^{2})}{{x}^{3}y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=1-x{y}^{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278250 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05f76324-5a68-5230-a5cd-bf08feffd775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275530} {:answer/id #uuid "89f30304-64a1-56ba-bd73-bcc48e23b10a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276724} {:answer/id #uuid "9562c48d-8b5b-53a4-9421-210d904f36b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276823} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ad9708-221f-5829-9e8f-6b54521f34fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276941} {:answer/id #uuid "dd43b247-ee16-5db2-b7b2-06fdc79123a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2ad9708-221f-5829-9e8f-6b54521f34fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276941} :answer-field/id #uuid "d372165d-773c-522b-a6ae-4635a798bcf6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7c4ebeea-f58f-5eb8-93aa-37b6d0eeb259" :question/math-academy-id "q-159716" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ for $f(x,y)={x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x{y}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-{y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) & =(\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x))-{y}^{3}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =((4{x}^{3})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{x}^{4}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x))-{y}^{3} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{x}^{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69e44334-00de-5702-83e5-16a7570d043c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(2x+y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276427} {:answer/id #uuid "8aac973e-8257-545d-b095-ab149936e003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276733} {:answer/id #uuid "b7cf2fa9-6053-5c4d-852e-474c37939e76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277108} {:answer/id #uuid "dd338f07-9cf2-51fd-a11c-32c271645616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1+x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277414} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b315c7-d154-5db9-8a29-731dc66826e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-x{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd338f07-9cf2-51fd-a11c-32c271645616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1+x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277414} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c3c66f0-c7ef-59da-9462-dd34d39d1caf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "485c686b-8a53-5bf0-8bc4-72a915a1ba56" :question/math-academy-id "q-159723" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-{y}^{2}}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{x-{y}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot (x-{y}^{2})-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-{y}^{2})}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y\\cdot (x-{y}^{2})-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot (-2y)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy-2{y}^{3}+2{x}^{2}y+2{y}^{3}}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy+2{x}^{2}y}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xy(1+x)}{{(x-{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=2xy(1+x).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278254 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47d515c6-7925-5320-a23c-240a300aec93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276111} {:answer/id #uuid "5d686b90-3df8-52b1-80bd-25c137cc92e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276311} {:answer/id #uuid "60c10891-1d7b-5e75-a24f-b405299f1c94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276345} {:answer/id #uuid "90b73919-9597-5b2d-970e-88b31b287e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276790} {:answer/id #uuid "e26f7a61-188b-57c0-b352-c69a4a8d07d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e26f7a61-188b-57c0-b352-c69a4a8d07d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277459} :answer-field/id #uuid "b11e4e9d-db09-5e46-8d26-27def32836dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fd55c472-88b5-5201-8165-4111e38766b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-159752" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\sqrt{y},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(\\frac{1}{4},4).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product, the chain, and the constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) & =(\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)))+\\sqrt{y}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =(1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+x\\cdot \\frac{1}{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy))+\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x))+\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+1+\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\frac{1}{4},4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(1/4,4)} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4)+1+\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+1+2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278259 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "279e76f9-f9f0-5564-ae7c-148de9a68761" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275840} {:answer/id #uuid "4db3fc28-5e05-5ec0-9cc6-98a0f4ab9c44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276163} {:answer/id #uuid "55ba531b-b121-55b8-9aa2-75e80c2df8e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276239} {:answer/id #uuid "9ad34d84-aa0e-5791-b041-c5ef3f6d8bab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276864} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d1bcdc-b7ea-5e71-b840-58edcde3907f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55ba531b-b121-55b8-9aa2-75e80c2df8e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276239} :answer-field/id #uuid "57d1b1f3-769f-55bc-82da-be45d6d73f43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277882}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3f9cc492-b3ba-556f-a019-182cbc410bcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-159766" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},$ evaluate ${f}_{y}(2,\\sqrt{5}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the chain, the sum, and the constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) & =1\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+y\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot ({x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(1)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\cdot ({x}^{2}\\cdot 0+2y) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,\\sqrt{5}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(2,\\sqrt{5})} & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}+\\frac{{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+5}+\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{4+5}} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{5}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278260 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a78e326-4c51-50ac-aad3-5c443d334667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275864} {:answer/id #uuid "5bbfe750-2540-5243-bc59-e0f79dc31902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276300} {:answer/id #uuid "6a035055-68f4-5be4-adae-4803c1279845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276429} {:answer/id #uuid "8b99f649-3f43-5a3f-8b56-e0ddedb38c57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3+\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276746} {:answer/id #uuid "9ca8f984-ab7a-5d4f-91f6-049dec25f1e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a78e326-4c51-50ac-aad3-5c443d334667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275864} :answer-field/id #uuid "f21cf5ea-df9a-5241-8868-5373b87209ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e7a86e6a-207f-552d-b9da-b1e5c673da4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-159768" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(2,\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) & =x(\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =x(1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡y+y\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y))+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(2,\\pi )} & =2\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\  & =2(-1-\\pi \\cdot 0)+(-1) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323711 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "359742a6-8a0e-5705-b305-bdbfab09ad97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(x+1)^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321557} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e8e21f-dd05-54d4-9135-759212c11a07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322582} {:answer/id #uuid "baf21348-aa27-59ef-b997-7967d7ce27a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y(x+1)^{2y-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322597} {:answer/id #uuid "c728a1b6-53de-52b8-9756-83f9687e51da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322691} {:answer/id #uuid "d6641433-9b61-5746-a0f6-b80a7538be32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c728a1b6-53de-52b8-9756-83f9687e51da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322691} :answer-field/id #uuid "e72f75b7-2611-5c69-b6cd-8d8554967419" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9932dc44-faa7-51c4-b14b-b1d882efadd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-35713" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ for $f(x,y)=(x+1)^{{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x+1)^{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the sum rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+1) & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1)) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\cdot (1+0) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(x+1)^{{y}^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323712 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "206738b8-5b84-547e-9fc3-5c5d89f2d22c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321393} {:answer/id #uuid "22f21454-5045-5e7c-9bd3-5be290d34f9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z-(z+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321413} {:answer/id #uuid "247c8ed0-8058-5736-99fc-d402a62c5d95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321429} {:answer/id #uuid "46f5a4e6-b0ae-5172-87cf-4dfb5cdbd0f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321706} {:answer/id #uuid "afe19fe2-9ce8-59b2-84b2-a3c39bdb418d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afe19fe2-9ce8-59b2-84b2-a3c39bdb418d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322526} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f75b94c-9bc5-56e1-980b-18e918de3927" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "233491ec-5789-55b3-aaad-7e685a7ed619" :question/math-academy-id "q-35721" :question/problem "Find ${g}_{z}(x,y,z)$ for $g(x,y,z)=(x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+(z+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $z,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}((x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+(z+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}((x+y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}((z+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =(x+y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡z)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(z+y) \\\\  & =(x+y)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =(x+y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡z+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335761 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ce3b46d-4467-59a9-895b-8e79ecd42cbc" :answer/type {:db/i