orname{cos}⁡(\\pi (1)) \\\\  & =8-2(1)(-1) \\\\  & =8+2 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436604 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cedb0ea-68aa-5297-8739-1c67694130cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436545} {:answer/id #uuid "89c32784-67a9-5a3f-9541-f6b61f434ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436554} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f43775-fb77-555a-84a3-313713b28808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436575} {:answer/id #uuid "cef87b38-87f4-5c33-ae55-63daa3d3acae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436577} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0a7424-1567-5720-902e-f99517a66dc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cedb0ea-68aa-5297-8739-1c67694130cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436545} :answer-field/id #uuid "4182c953-888a-5a78-b08a-c5df63ce2717" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0d55bb11-970c-5f1f-831a-44fb97e659c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-132261" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)={cos}^{2}⁡(3x-{y}^{2}),$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(0,\\sqrt{\\pi }).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({cos}^{2}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x-{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\cdot (3x\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\cdot (3x\\cdot 0-2y) \\\\  & =4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,\\sqrt{\\pi }):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(0,\\sqrt{\\pi })} & =4(\\sqrt{\\pi })\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3(0)-{(\\sqrt{\\pi })}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3(0)-{(\\sqrt{\\pi })}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi ) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dde26e5-909a-5520-b5a4-d567f4f30d3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436556} {:answer/id #uuid "8e6e21a7-d420-5add-b68c-d19db196b561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436559} {:answer/id #uuid "ab23a96c-3799-57cf-a6c2-1ae6ae0bc1c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436568} {:answer/id #uuid "c12523e2-dee4-5166-961f-0a9b274f76d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436573} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a4e0d8-9189-5dce-8c93-80f07feaa44f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dde26e5-909a-5520-b5a4-d567f4f30d3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436556} :answer-field/id #uuid "1990b86b-b897-5e01-b1d1-8c99349fdebe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "26e723d1-2e7d-5b20-b4fd-e3325c571238" :question/math-academy-id "q-159696" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{3xy-1}{2x-3y},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(0,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{3xy-1}{2x-3y}\\right) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3xy-1)\\cdot (2x-3y)-(3xy-1)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x-3y)}{(2x-3y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x\\cdot (2x-3y)-(3xy-1)\\cdot (-3)}{(2x-3y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{x}^{2}-9xy+9xy-3}{(2x-3y)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{x}^{2}-3}{(2x-3y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,-1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(0,-1)} & =\\frac{6(0)^{2}-3}{(2(0)-3(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436606 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2eb1fcd4-1769-591e-b2b3-2926ae221a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{y}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436539} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5aa69d-a57a-53e7-a411-7b8d1e231bc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436542} {:answer/id #uuid "8397e509-d007-5ca5-ab7f-b6777f6c8813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436551} {:answer/id #uuid "898b4cbe-f73a-573e-8210-8119141fd3d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436553} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f7930b-c4f8-5a1e-9abf-4982ea59ffa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8397e509-d007-5ca5-ab7f-b6777f6c8813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436551} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf6e9e9d-4e43-54d1-b414-a2a8e2b2fbf9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "27e4d0e6-6215-57d4-b123-69cd51f3932f" :question/math-academy-id "q-159720" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{e}^{xy}}{xy}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{h(x,y){e}^{xy}}{{x}^{2}y}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient and chain rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{{e}^{xy}}{xy}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy})\\cdot xy-{e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)}{(xy)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)\\cdot xy-{e}^{xy}\\cdot y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{xy}\\cdot y\\cdot xy-y{e}^{xy}}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y{e}^{xy}(xy-1)}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(xy-1){e}^{xy}}{{x}^{2}y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=xy-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436607 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2979f6ee-54a4-596c-a00e-b93729a2aa3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436536} {:answer/id #uuid "2ca6a6cc-0e50-532f-b694-62c94e10b39b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436537} {:answer/id #uuid "8deb0301-83cb-5ae4-a55a-80df750a6116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436557} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a2557a-94f8-59b3-b60d-cf6d567bf8a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436565} {:answer/id #uuid "cb9d30be-a6d6-5be3-8d4c-d3456b4912f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2979f6ee-54a4-596c-a00e-b93729a2aa3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436536} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ff5ffb8-ede5-57b1-913a-ec470f862cc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436598}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "45d0ef52-763b-56d4-b138-648452f050d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-132258" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)={e}^{4y-x{z}^{4}},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(4,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{4y-x{z}^{4}}) \\\\  & ={e}^{4y-x{z}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4y-x{z}^{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the sum and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4y-x{z}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(4y-x{z}^{4}) & ={e}^{4y-x{z}^{4}}\\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4y)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{z}^{4})) \\\\  & ={e}^{4y-x{z}^{4}}\\cdot (0-{z}^{4}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)) \\\\  & ={e}^{4y-x{z}^{4}}\\cdot (-{z}^{4})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-{z}^{4}{e}^{4y-x{z}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(4,1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂z}{|}_{(4,1,1)} & =-(1)^{4}{e}^{4(1)-4(1)^{4}} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436608 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07492d45-331a-54bb-8e47-f1b2b223890f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436532} {:answer/id #uuid "19558a15-5391-55ca-be3a-0060eedc7548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436534} {:answer/id #uuid "222c0ad5-80fe-5476-9e00-ff1bd21126b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436535} {:answer/id #uuid "e8cb64e1-7f9f-5311-8f6d-68fccffe0505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436583} {:answer/id #uuid "e948a45c-9ad5-5281-8231-163c228a69e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8cb64e1-7f9f-5311-8f6d-68fccffe0505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436583} :answer-field/id #uuid "23ccffc7-1099-5214-9516-b32cd1948e7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6c44dfc3-39f6-598a-be48-62e051abdda4" :question/math-academy-id "q-70029" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=(2y+1)^{2x+1},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((2y+1)^{2x+1}) \\\\  & =(2x+1)(2y+1)^{2x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}((2y+1))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(2x+1)(2y+1)^{2x}\\cdot (2\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1)) \\\\  & =(2x+1)(2y+1)^{2x}\\cdot (2\\cdot 1+0) \\\\  & =2(2x+1)(2y+1)^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(2,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(2,0)} & =2\\cdot (2\\cdot 2+1)\\cdot (2\\cdot 0+1)^{2\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5\\cdot {1}^{4} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436609 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "124ea6fa-c270-53e3-9a4a-37fa95f78b09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}(2x+{x}^{3}){e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436533} {:answer/id #uuid "7056dc0c-db4a-59ad-96ec-55d08cc43675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{2}{x}^{3}{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436549} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd16539-0ba2-553c-a354-7862eff2dcad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{2}(x+{x}^{3}){e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436555} {:answer/id #uuid "9b415193-f30e-568c-b97e-366ae0eaaea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{2}(x+2{x}^{2}){e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436562} {:answer/id #uuid "9cfa64ff-4036-5039-b10a-3ab9558904ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{2}x{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bd16539-0ba2-553c-a354-7862eff2dcad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{2}(x+{x}^{3}){e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436555} :answer-field/id #uuid "aae5189e-28a0-5ea3-8961-0076527201e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a1fee486-b1a7-59bd-ae9a-400ceeb58414" :question/math-academy-id "q-159715" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the constant multiple rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product rule and the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}}) & ={y}^{2}(\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{{x}^{2}}+{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{{x}^{2}})) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}((2x)\\cdot {e}^{{x}^{2}}+{x}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(2x{e}^{{x}^{2}}+{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\cdot (2x)) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}(2x{e}^{{x}^{2}}+2{x}^{3}{e}^{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =2{y}^{2}(x+{x}^{3}){e}^{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436610 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2da9aa45-1bc3-5a50-8a63-b565f85bcbad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436538} {:answer/id #uuid "52dadf7c-60d4-59bf-a211-32c2a6e0ff88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436544} {:answer/id #uuid "6d9bf8eb-7a93-55c9-a108-2de82f52459e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436548} {:answer/id #uuid "a42fffab-44a5-5b6b-b508-53d3e76d2912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436566} {:answer/id #uuid "be5d2acc-cc2d-528d-9424-532714fcefa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2da9aa45-1bc3-5a50-8a63-b565f85bcbad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436538} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f0051c2-f01a-525a-9309-c47735be89a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a235487c-a19a-5a88-ae3b-cb08ed11bcd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-132251" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)$ for $f(x,y,z)={cos}^{2}⁡(3x-{y}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({cos}^{2}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2}))\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(3x-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2}))\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-{y}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x-{y}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436611 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "738f363f-7faa-5ab8-9897-b5ae98173bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4})+4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436550} {:answer/id #uuid "a92787e6-66cd-5569-b00d-1c269f0cc548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436567} {:answer/id #uuid "e35b52fb-dc96-5d35-81e4-c054d2cd8c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4})+4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436581} {:answer/id #uuid "f3882228-8779-5c90-80d2-5aebfcddf4d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436587} {:answer/id #uuid "f700fd99-e71c-5d3f-aa39-098cd2e2c465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4})+2y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e35b52fb-dc96-5d35-81e4-c054d2cd8c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4})+4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436581} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fb83488-f3c3-5970-b632-d70d187404f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436592}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "aaa7facc-73c8-58b5-b03f-ad80dd8597f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-159691" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the constant multiple rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4})) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the product and the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4})) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4})+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4})) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot (1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4})+y\\cdot \\frac{1}{{y}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{4})) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4})+\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}\\cdot (4{y}^{3}))) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{4})+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436612 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a29d2d7f-53ec-597d-89a7-86301ab042db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436564} {:answer/id #uuid "b7315fa2-8e78-5d6e-ae0d-d1ac80caf4b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{x}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436570} {:answer/id #uuid "c1e3f11a-2a92-578b-8110-66edfa5a659d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{xy}-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436574} {:answer/id #uuid "e45462b7-70a5-5766-8cbb-438381842509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436582} {:answer/id #uuid "f705c608-1802-5751-bc1d-6461a3354b31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{xy}-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e45462b7-70a5-5766-8cbb-438381842509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436582} :answer-field/id #uuid "750b8f34-0f9d-56c2-985a-b6e255c43f41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436599}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b72fd759-0cb1-5717-8778-6af4e6d7337a" :question/math-academy-id "q-159653" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ for $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)-xy.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)-xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the chain rule and the constant multiple rules for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy))-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yx) & =\\frac{1}{xy}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yx) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{xy}\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{xy}\\cdot y\\cdot 1-y\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}-y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436613 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49517556-0d0e-548e-a3c1-8430dc1612ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436543} {:answer/id #uuid "92355996-2538-5d06-adbb-60fbc547dfd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436560} {:answer/id #uuid "d25dbf87-9ff4-5222-983d-a08125cb25b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436578} {:answer/id #uuid "d9cd43b3-1131-5c70-bf1e-5c97871cb3df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436579} {:answer/id #uuid "f122d57b-621e-5f14-a573-0116c8efb68e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d25dbf87-9ff4-5222-983d-a08125cb25b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436578} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b91fb5a-fb60-5758-b55c-b8f8d909486c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436596}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f311e12c-1089-5d71-97f6-83e1fd9c3339" :question/math-academy-id "q-159702" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{y}},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{y}}\\right) & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\cdot \\sqrt{y}-({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{y})}{{(\\sqrt{y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2y\\cdot \\sqrt{y}-({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}})}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{4{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\right)}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}}{2y\\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(3,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(3,1)} & =\\frac{{3}^{2}+3(1)^{2}}{2(1)\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9+3}{2} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436614 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cc88c0d-b906-5169-8020-771089d1d342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+7y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436541} {:answer/id #uuid "6a8f703d-08c4-5364-a106-a8206935b823" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-11y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436547} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2c81c3-bd1b-576f-8ea5-5e15ecc6a989" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x-22y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436558} {:answer/id #uuid "9aa74480-20e7-5b9c-bfdf-57f701ad6150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11y-6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436561} {:answer/id #uuid "f4bd98b7-39d1-5926-929c-4305a2b89c9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+11y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9aa74480-20e7-5b9c-bfdf-57f701ad6150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11y-6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436561} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba8cfa2f-c627-57d0-923a-8380a85a57e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f88992c6-7672-5688-a790-113b251f1d96" :question/math-academy-id "q-159721" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{6x+11y}{\\sqrt{y}}.$ The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{h(x,y)}{2y\\sqrt{y}}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{6x+11y}{\\sqrt{y}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{∂}{∂y}(6x+11y)\\cdot \\sqrt{y}-(6x+11y)\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{y})}{{(\\sqrt{y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(11\\cdot \\sqrt{y}-(6x+11y)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}})}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(\\frac{22y-(6x+11y)}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\right)}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{11y-6x}{2y\\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=11y-6x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436615 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c938da8-22ab-5a7b-8a0c-e429c22edff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{82}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436540} {:answer/id #uuid "618a305e-63e4-5e63-9489-f0e69a8d45f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436546} {:answer/id #uuid "884b828b-42b8-5163-ae82-8d67dc83a64c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436552} {:answer/id #uuid "adda18f8-69d7-5871-aba2-4a24c35225f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{80}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436569} {:answer/id #uuid "b77fca6c-dc77-556b-8294-ff448ec939d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c938da8-22ab-5a7b-8a0c-e429c22edff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{82}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436540} :answer-field/id #uuid "e47d5957-7c5b-50d5-a6fa-3e6133a8dcdf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fe49ff44-a8f4-5323-af29-4e99b3a5291b" :question/math-academy-id "q-159663" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x{y}^{2}),$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the chain rule: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x{y}^{2}))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{(x{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the constant multiple rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\cdot {y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\cdot {y}^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,3)} & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{1+{1}^{2}\\cdot {3}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{1+81} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{82}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566225 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a507ce6-22ce-56f0-ba53-527362e98081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x^{3}+16xy^{2}-16x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a507ce6-22ce-56f0-ba53-527362e98081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x^{3}+16xy^{2}-16x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565924} :answer-field/id #uuid "5406b9c4-8f08-5b5f-8ea0-96705a9a7215" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4d7ebf34-a035-5c2e-ad76-841acaa3c221" :question/math-academy-id "q-168886" :question/problem "$\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-8{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{4})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8{x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8{x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{4})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8{x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the constant multiple rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{4})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8{x}^{2}{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8{x}^{2}) & =2\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{4})+8{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})-8\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4{x}^{3}+8{y}^{2}\\cdot 2x-8\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =8{x}^{3}+16x{y}^{2}-16x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3687686f-27d7-5790-b17c-25679b2d1bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{y}^{x-1}-{z}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566472} {:answer/id #uuid "98ba232a-4707-557a-b5e6-2e7896a3faba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{y}^{x-1}-3y{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566662} {:answer/id #uuid "b619f3ad-5474-53a1-863a-0d77cd05c096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{x-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-{z}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566721} {:answer/id #uuid "b787c94d-cc66-56fe-ab2f-bae4827c49ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3y{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566727} {:answer/id #uuid "d90c9bfa-7951-5e10-bace-6cd8713f434a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3687686f-27d7-5790-b17c-25679b2d1bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{y}^{x-1}-{z}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566472} :answer-field/id #uuid "31a1c922-50b2-51e3-a611-69b79808fdf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "059319c8-1dff-5dfe-8695-5074282cdfe9" :question/math-academy-id "q-132248" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{y}(x,y,z)$ for $f(x,y,z)={y}^{x}-y{z}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nUsing the sum and constant multiple rules, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{x}-y{z}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{x})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{z}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{x})-{z}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =x{y}^{x-1}-{z}^{3}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =x{y}^{x-1}-{z}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0163c90f-63f7-520c-b90b-cdca85bc5861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566364} {:answer/id #uuid "78d2aa47-e366-536d-979b-7aaddb43183d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566591} {:answer/id #uuid "90f591ac-d503-53e4-9edf-df0ecead1c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566647} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8aa054-536b-5175-8e3d-21f8ecd92148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566710} {:answer/id #uuid "c62a4f9c-30eb-5f