\partial f}{\\partial y}$, where $x - y^{2} + 1\\ne0$." :question/worked-solution "Hold $x$ constant and differentiate with respect to $y$. Write $N=e^{- x y^{2}}$ and $D=x - y^{2} + 1$. The component derivatives are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN_{y}&=- 2 x y e^{- x y^{2}}, \\\\\nD_{y}&=- 2 y.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule differentiates the exponent first; its inner derivative is $- 2 x y$. Apply the quotient rule, keeping its subtraction and squared denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{N_{y}D-ND_{y}}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\left(- 2 x y e^{- x y^{2}}\\right)D-N\\left(- 2 y\\right)}{D^2} \\\\\n&=\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} - 2 x y + 2 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2} + 1\\right)^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last step factors the common nonzero exponential $e^{- x y^{2}}$ from the numerator.  These expressions apply where $x - y^{2} + 1\\ne0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703576 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "453d9798-d79d-5357-b594-39c83563a78c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{2} y + 2 x y^{3} + 2 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2}\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703586} {:answer/id #uuid "4e21f254-b085-56ba-b52d-0510163f8767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(- 2 x^{3} y + 4 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x y^{5} + 2 x y - 2 y^{3}\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2}\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703587} {:answer/id #uuid "b8741453-4ca9-579e-adb2-a32b6cc2a070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(2 y\\right)}{\\left(x - y^{2}\\right)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703595} {:answer/id #uuid "ba1686a8-0609-5876-9d71-8ec3a13cd105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{- x y^{2}}\\left(